module

public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Functors.Module.ExactSupport
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.RingedSpace.ModulePullbackUnit
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Generators
import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorAlgebraPullback

/-!
# The unit of `f^* ⊣ f_*` is an epimorphism on globally generated modules

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion of ringed spaces. [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3] part (1)
asserts that for a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules `M` the unit

`η_M : M ⟶ i_* i^* M`

is an epimorphism with kernel `ℐ M`, the first half being the statement that
`i_* i^* M = M ⊗_{𝒪_X} i_* 𝒪_Z` is generated by the image of `M`. This file proves epimorphy of
`η_M` whenever `M` is generated by global sections, with no tensor product anywhere: the proof
is the generator argument, in three steps.

1. At `M = 𝒪_X` the unit *is* the comorphism `i^♯`, by
   `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.unit_app_unit`, so it is an epimorphism exactly because
   `i^♯` is surjective. This is the generator formula: a section `a` goes to `a ⊗ 1 = i^♯(a)`.
2. At `M = 𝒪_X^{(I)}` free, the pullback is free on the same index type
   (`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullbackObjFreeIso`) and `i_*` preserves the coproduct, so
   the unit is a coproduct of copies of `i^♯`.
3. Epimorphy of the unit propagates along an epimorphism `N ⟶ M`, by naturality, provided
   `i_* i^*` preserves epimorphisms.

Steps 2 and 3 need `i_*` to preserve coproducts and epimorphisms, and what supplies that is
*not* the exactness of pushforward of [Stacks Project, Tag 01AX]: it is the adjunction of
[Stacks Project, Tag 0A75] — see
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.ClosedQuotientMorphismOfRingedSpaces.isLeftAdjoint_modulePushforward`
— which exhibits `i_*` on sheaves of *modules* as a **left** adjoint, of sheaf Hom with exact
support. A left adjoint preserves all colimits. Tag 01AX is proved in the library only for
sheaves of abelian groups and is not used here.

Accordingly the results below take the two properties of `i` as instance hypotheses,
`Epi (structureSheafModuleHom i)` and `(modulePushforward i).IsLeftAdjoint`, rather than any
one packaging of "closed immersion": the first is a defining field of
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsClosedImmersion` and the second a theorem about
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.ClosedQuotientMorphismOfRingedSpaces`, and nothing in the library
relates those two packagings.

## Main results

* `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.isLeftAdjoint_modulePullback`: `f^*` is a left adjoint for
  every morphism of ringed spaces, as an instance, hence preserves epimorphisms.
* `ClosedQuotientMorphismOfRingedSpaces.isLeftAdjoint_modulePushforward`: `i_*` is a left
  adjoint for a closed quotient morphism of ringed spaces, as an instance.
* `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.ιFree_comp_homEquiv_pullbackObjFreeIso_hom`: the generator
  formula on a free sheaf of modules — on the `j`-th summand the comparison is `i^♯`.
* `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_free`: the unit is an epimorphism at a free
  sheaf of modules.
* `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_of_generatingSections`: the unit is an
  epimorphism at any sheaf of modules generated by global sections.

## Implementation notes

`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.free I` is the coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf indexed
by `I`, and step 2 is run through the colimit cofan rather than through a chosen isomorphism
`i_*(𝒪_Z^{(I)}) ≅ (i_* 𝒪_Z)^{(I)}`: the family `i_*(ιFree j)` is jointly epimorphic because
`i_*` preserves the coproduct, and that is all that is used.

The proofs are written with `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction` and
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullback` rather than with
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction` and
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePullback`. The two are equal by `rfl`, but the latter are
`def`s and so do not unfold at the `implicit` transparency at which `rw` checks that a motive is
type-correct; every rewrite in `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_free` fails if
the Mathlib spelling is replaced by the repo one. The statements are nevertheless given in the
repo spelling, and the passage between them is by `exact`, at which default transparency
applies.

What is **not** proved here is the case of a sheaf of modules that is only *locally* generated,
which is what `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsClosedImmersion` supplies for an ideal sheaf
(`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData`). That needs epimorphy of a morphism of
sheaves of modules to be local on the base, which the library does not have.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01R3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A75](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A75)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0096](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0096)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.ClosedQuotientMorphismOfRingedSpaces

/-- **Pushforward of sheaves of modules along a closed quotient morphism of ringed spaces is a
left adjoint.** Its right adjoint is sheaf Hom with exact support, by [Stacks Project, Tag
0A75]. Registered as an instance: it is what makes `i_*` preserve epimorphisms and coproducts,
and so it is the hypothesis on `i` that the generator argument for [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3]
part (1) runs on. -/
instance isLeftAdjoint_modulePushforward (S : ClosedQuotientMorphismOfRingedSpaces.{u}) :
    (modulePushforward S.i).IsLeftAdjoint :=
  ⟨_, ⟨S.modulePushforwardSheafHomExactSupportAdjunction⟩⟩

end RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.ClosedQuotientMorphismOfRingedSpaces

namespace RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

variable {X Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- **The generator formula on a free sheaf of modules.** Read on the `j`-th summand of
`𝒪_Y^{(I)}`, the transpose of the identification
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.pullbackObjFreeIso` of `f^*(𝒪_Y^{(I)})` with `𝒪_X^{(I)}` is the
comorphism of structure sheaves followed by `f_*` of the inclusion of the `j`-th summand.

This is the free analogue of `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.unit_app_unit`, and it is what
makes the comparison on a free module a coproduct of copies of `f^♯` rather than an unidentified
isomorphism. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem ιFree_comp_homEquiv_pullbackObjFreeIso_hom (I : Type u) (j : I) :
    SheafOfModules.ιFree j ≫
        (SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (structureSheafHom f)).homEquiv _ _
          (SheafOfModules.pullbackObjFreeIso (structureSheafHom f) I).hom =
      structureSheafModuleHom f ≫
        (SheafOfModules.pushforward (structureSheafHom f)).map (SheafOfModules.ιFree j) := by
  rw [← Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_left,
    SheafOfModules.pullback_map_ιFree_comp_pullbackObjFreeIso_hom,
    Adjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right,
    SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction_homEquiv_pullbackObjUnitToUnit]
  rfl

/-- **The unit of `f^* ⊣ f_*` is an epimorphism at a free sheaf of modules**, when the
comorphism of structure sheaves is an epimorphism and `f_*` is a left adjoint.

By `RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.ιFree_comp_homEquiv_pullbackObjFreeIso_hom` the
comparison is, on each summand, the comorphism of structure sheaves; and the family of summand
inclusions of `f_*(𝒪_X^{(I)})` is jointly epimorphic because `f_*`, being a left adjoint,
preserves the coproduct. -/
theorem epi_unit_app_free [Epi (structureSheafModuleHom f)]
    [(modulePushforward f).IsLeftAdjoint] (I : Type u) :
    Epi ((modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app (SheafOfModules.free I)) := by
  have : (SheafOfModules.pushforward (structureSheafHom f)).IsLeftAdjoint :=
    inferInstanceAs (modulePushforward f).IsLeftAdjoint
  have hι : Epi ((SheafOfModules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (structureSheafHom f)).homEquiv _ _
      (SheafOfModules.pullbackObjFreeIso (structureSheafHom f) I).hom) := by
    refine ⟨fun u v huv => ?_⟩
    have key : ∀ j : I, (SheafOfModules.pushforward (structureSheafHom f)).map
        (SheafOfModules.ιFree j) ≫ u =
        (SheafOfModules.pushforward (structureSheafHom f)).map (SheafOfModules.ιFree j) ≫ v :=
      fun j => (cancel_epi (structureSheafModuleHom f)).mp
        ((ιFree_comp_homEquiv_pullbackObjFreeIso_hom_assoc f I j u).symm.trans
          ((congrArg (SheafOfModules.ιFree j ≫ ·) huv).trans
            (ιFree_comp_homEquiv_pullbackObjFreeIso_hom_assoc f I j v)))
    exact Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext (isColimitCofanMkObjOfIsColimit
      (SheafOfModules.pushforward (structureSheafHom f)) _ _
      (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan (R := structureSheafRing X) I)) u v key
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit] at hι
  exact (epi_comp_iff_of_isIso _ ((SheafOfModules.pushforward (structureSheafHom f)).map
    (SheafOfModules.pullbackObjFreeIso (structureSheafHom f) I).hom)).mp hι

/-- **The unit of `f^* ⊣ f_*` is an epimorphism at a sheaf of modules generated by global
sections.** This is the first half of the second assertion of [Stacks Project, Tag 01R3] part
(1) for a globally generated module: the image of `M` generates
`f_* f^* M = M ⊗_{𝒪_Y} f_* 𝒪_X`.

The generators are used only through the epimorphism
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.π : 𝒪_Y^{(I)} ⟶ M`, along which
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_of_epi` transports
`RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.epi_unit_app_free`. -/
theorem epi_unit_app_of_generatingSections [Epi (structureSheafModuleHom f)]
    [(modulePushforward f).IsLeftAdjoint] {M : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y)}
    (σ : M.GeneratingSections) :
    Epi ((modulePullbackPushforwardAdjunction f).unit.app M) :=
  epi_unit_app_of_epi f σ.π (epi_unit_app_free f σ.I) inferInstance

end RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

end
